    {
      "id": "daedalus-process",
      "type": "text",
      "width": "full",
      "heading": "From script to reader",
      "body": "The process moved from story and script to source-image selection and cleanup, page design in Figma, panel animation in Rive, and a reader state machine with JavaScript progression. The central challenge was maintaining continuity across inconsistent source material.",
      "source": "",
      "mediaRef": "",
      "href": "",
      "label": "",
      "projectId": "",
      "alt": "",
      "fit": "cover"
    },
    {
      "id": "daedalus-reception",
      "type": "text",
      "width": "full",
      "heading": "How I introduced the project",
      "body": "A process-led post reached 9K views. A later post about the personal reason for making the comic reached 2.0M views, 3,417 upvotes, and 236 comments. These were different posts, not a controlled comparison.\n\nThe contrast changed how I introduced the work: personal motivation first, production process second.",
      "source": "",
      "mediaRef": "",
      "href": "",
      "label": "",
      "projectId": "",
      "alt": "",
      "fit": "cover"
    },
